cff-version: 1.2.0
message: 'If you use BarelySig in your research, please cite it as below.'
type: software
title: 'BarelySig'
abstract: "Free, open-source statistics and graphing for wet-lab scientists, in the browser. Column and Grouped tables with paste from spreadsheets; t tests, Mann-Whitney and Wilcoxon tests, one- and two-way ANOVA with multiple comparisons, Kruskal-Wallis with Dunn's test and normality tests, computed by R (WebR) and validated against desktop R; bar, dot, box, violin and grouped bar graphs with significance brackets, exported as SVG or PNG at journal sizes with a reproducible recipe. All computation is client-side."
authors:
  - family-names: Usaj
    given-names: Matej
    email: m.usaj@utoronto.ca
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0675-2847'
    affiliation: 'The Donnelly Centre, University of Toronto'
license: MIT
repository-code: 'https://github.com/BooneAndrewsLab/BarelySig'
url: 'https://booneandrewslab.github.io/BarelySig/'
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-25
keywords:
  - statistics
  - graphing
  - GraphPad Prism alternative
  - t test
  - ANOVA
  - significance
  - WebR
  - reproducibility
